{% comment %}
  A lift model. The page opens with the model name and its strapline.

  Titles are stored as "The Donnington: Car Parking / Stacking Lift" — the
  `name` and `strapline` fields split that so the heading can lead with the
  model name and set the descriptor underneath, while the document title stays
  intact for search results and the browser tab.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  Two-column layout: the main column carries the galleries, overview and
  description in normal reading order; a sticky sidebar carries the
  specification sheet (grouped into a few titled spec-list blocks — see
  site/content/product/*.json's "regions.sidebar") so a reader never has to
  scroll away from the numbers to keep reading, or vice versa. FAQs and
  related products (regions.related) run full-width below both columns.

  This replaces an earlier tabbed layout, and then a tab-free single-scroll
  layout with a sticky jump nav — both tried and moved on from. No nav bar
  here: with specs always visible in the sidebar, there's nothing left that
  needs jumping to.
{% endcomment %}
<article class="content post tpl-product">
  <header class="content__header content__narrow anim-hidden">
    <h1 class="content__title">{{ doc.title | escape }}</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="product-layout">
    <div class="product-main">
      {% region 'content' %}
    </div>
    <aside class="product-sidebar">
      {% region 'sidebar' %}
    </aside>
  </div>

  <div class="product-full">
    {% region 'related' %}
  </div>
</article>
